export anchor TestProgress:
    description:
        Before the first test starts, a line on stderr names the agent and the
        model that judge the tests, like judging with claude, model opus, or
        says that the agent uses its default model, like judging with claude,
        default model. It is written at once, not kept until the end like a
        note, so it shows while the tests run.

        A test can take minutes, so a run never sits silent while one is being
        judged. On a terminal, a status block below the results is redrawn as
        things change: a spinner with how many tests are done and running, then
        one line per running test with its name, how long it has been running,
        and what its tool did last. Results are printed above the block as they
        finish, and the block is gone when the run ends.

        What a tool did last comes from its output as it is written. Claude's
        events name its tool calls, like reading crates/piton-cli/src/main.rs or
        searching spec for a pattern, with paths relative to the project, and
        the first line of what it says; it reads thinking while it works on its
        first turn. For the other tools it is the last line they printed.

        When stderr isn't a terminal, a block would only clutter a log, so a
        line saying running and the test's name is written as each test starts
        instead.
